change and is told make test excludes integration, contradicting the new behavior and re-opening the same trust gap the ticket exists to close"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add `.agents/rules/rebar.md` and `infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md` to the Scope/Docs edit set (and review docs/coverage.md), updating each 'make test excludes integration' statement to reflect that make test now runs the default tier and then the integration tier.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the gating cell's selection is genuinely a superset of every other cell in the `test` job's matrix (after `exclude`) — in particular that no cell runs `external`-marked tests the gating cell excludes — or scope the superset claim to the markers actually present in the matrix.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","COH"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: make test runs `-m \"not integration and not external\" ...` — gating cell excludes external","AC3: '...and form a superset of every matrix cell'","'for every cell in the job's matrix (after exclude), every truth assignment ... is also selected by some make test expression'"],"finding":"The plan introduces two jointly-required tests — equality (Makefile selection == gating cell's two pytest steps, which exclude `external`) and superset-of-every-matrix-cell — but does not establish that the gating cell's selection actually is a superset of every other matrix cell after `exclude`. If any non-gating cell in the `test` job selects `external` tests (which the gating cell's `not integration and not external` excludes), the superset test would fail and AC2+AC3 become jointly unsatisfiable without changing `make test`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f22c40de3889adef0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (superset test) and Acceptance Criteria 2 & 3","norm_id":"n22ac098e81e7d8e1","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A matrix cell exists whose DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS includes external-marked tests the gating cell does not run, making the superset test red and unfixable without editing make test"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to Approach step 2 recording that the `test` job's matrix cells (after exclude) only select subsets of `not integration and not external` plus `integration`, so the gating cell is a true superset; if a cell selects `external`, state how the superset test accounts for it.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the cell-selection helper extracts the marker expression from BOTH the literal `-m integration` form and the `-m \"$VAR\"` env-resolved form, and state what it does for a pytest step carrying no `-m` at all.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5413,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml line 763 default step: `pytest -m \"$DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS\"` (env-var form, DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS at line 755)",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml line 827 integration step: `pytest -m integration ... --dist loadgroup --max-worker-restart=0` (LITERAL marker, no env var)","Plan names only env-var resolution: 'resolving `-m \"$VAR\"` through the step's `env` matrix expression'"],"finding":"The cell-selection helper is specified to resolve only the `-m \"$VAR\"` env-var form, but the gating cell's integration step uses a LITERAL `-m integration` argument (no env var); the helper must extract both forms or it will miss/misparse the integration step's selection and the equality/superset assertions will not verify what AC2/AC3 claim.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff17937d8103ffaa1","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (first helper): \"resolving `-m \\\"$VAR\\\"` through the step's `env` matrix expression\"","norm_id":"n5c4166127cccf1e7","priority":0.0587,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Helper walks the test job's two